# Files a SOURCE analyser should not review, because they are not
# source: they are build output that this repository happens to commit.
#
# ts/dist and ts/dist-test are the compiled TypeScript (AGENTS.md
# explains why they are checked in, and CI has a staleness gate to keep
# them honest). Reviewing them reports every finding TWICE -- once
# against the line the author wrote and once against the line tsc
# emitted for it -- and reports transpiler artefacts as defects of code
# nobody wrote.
#
# web/aontu-bundle.js is the esbuild bundle of the same tree, minified,
# and says "Do not edit" in its first line.
#
# web/playground.html is that bundle again, inlined: the page is
# generated by web/build/build.mjs, which replaces ONE placeholder line
# in web/playground.template.html with the whole bundle text and
# changes nothing else ("everything else in the page is authored
# there"). Analysing it therefore reports the bundle's findings a THIRD
# time and the playground's own scripts a second.
#
# Everything a person writes is still analysed: ts/src, ts/test,
# web/build, and the playground's own scripts -- which live in
# web/playground.template.html, the file an author edits.
ts/dist/
ts/dist-test/
web/aontu-bundle.js
web/playground.html
